# ~/.profile.local  -*- mode: sh -*-
#
# Machine-local login-shell environment, NOT shared between machines.
# ~/.profile sources this file at its end. Login shells other than bash (e.g.
# dash on Linux) read ~/.profile too, so keep this file POSIX sh.
#
# The repository only tracks this commented template (added with `git add -f`);
# put real per-machine settings below it and never commit them.
#
# Once per clone, hide local edits from git:
#   git -C ~ update-index --skip-worktree .profile.local
# (undo with --no-skip-worktree, e.g. to update this template).
